{"text": "September 25, 2013\nDear Korean Community of Vi\n\n1 applaud your efforts to ensure that our school textbooks reflect an accurate\nunderstanding of history and geography in East Asia. The body of water known,\nalternately, as the East Sea or the Sea of Japan, should be properly labeled with both\nnames. As Governor. one of my most solemn responsibilities will be helping to reform\nVirginia's education system, and ensuring that our children\u2019s understanding of the world\nis accurate will be of paramount importance.\n\n| fully support efforts to use both names, East Sea/Sea of Japan, when used in maps or\ndescriptions in Virginia's textbooks. As Governor, I will ensure that as new texts are\npurchased or downloaded they reflect this important historical truth by supporting\nlegislation like that introduced by Democratic Senator Dave Marsden in 2012.\n\n\u2018Thank you for your dedication to our Commonwealth and for standing up for what you\nbeliew\n\nSincerely.\nrfiy\u2014\n\nTerry MeAuliffe.\n\nTerryMcAuliffe.com * (703) 822-7604 + PO Box 13881, Arlington, VA 22219\n\n(Pen torby Tey MeRai fr Govern\n\n<P",
